    "summary": "No record change. The remaining directions were considered rather than filed speculatively: the configuration mechanism (a new voter starts at Match 0, so it cannot contribute to a commit quorum, and its RecentActive starts true so an added node does not trigger a spurious quorum-check step-down), the removal path (a removed leader drops proposals because its own progress entry is gone, and its commit computation uses only the new quorum), and the append flow-control counters. Each follows from branches the account already cites, or has no reachable failure state that the surrounding code does not correct, so recording them would add vocabulary rather than change a judgment. The record set answers what was asked: one asserted defect (MsgForgetLeader absent from isLocalMsg, demonstrated on both documented inbound paths and reproduced on a second execution), a refuted progress-axis suspicion documented with its protective mechanism, eight supporting questions each carrying a hypothesis, a discriminator and an interpretation tied to receipts or cited ranges, one knowledge correction where a premise proved false, and the residual items stated as scope limits rather than open questions. No closing declaration is made, since that belongs to a preconfigured finite task or to the run boundary."
